# Execution Workflow Gates

- Follow sequence: plan -> interfaces -> implementation -> tests -> evidence -> docs update.
- Before coding, confirm target module boundary and acceptance criteria.
- Include tests for happy path, failure path, and retry/timeout behavior when relevant.
- Keep changes incremental; avoid big-bang rewrites unless explicitly approved.
- Keep code simple (KISS).
- For each task, define rollback/fallback behavior before merging.
- Block release when any P0 security/quality/reliability gate fails.
- Require deterministic replay tests for high-risk workflows and tool side effects.
- Require CI/CD evidence bundle links for release candidates.
- Update relevant research docs when architecture, policies, or runtime behavior changes.
